{
 "_why": "THE KILN WYRM's paths (DESIGN24-bosses.md section 1; builder B NIGHT24): a fixed learnable cycle of four patterns, each a waypoint list in ARENA-LOCAL metres (x, y, z; y up; the arena centre is 0, 0, 0 and the floor is y 0), smoothed by a Catmull-Rom spline, resampled to a constant arc length and pitch-clamped. Variant 0 is the west-dive cycle; variant 1 is its mirror in x. One variant is drawn per cycle from the run's seeded stream, for every pattern together, so the dive's exit side and the lunge's start side match. 'wp3' (the coil) is the waypoint list used in phase 3 (the squeeze closes the coil to a ring inside the pillars, cutting in through the gap between two of them). A mark is a moment on a pattern (a waypoint) with a tell: tell names a key of design.n24.wyrm.tells (seconds, never under 0.5), attack says it resolves as an attack (no two resolve inside tells.resolveGap), phase is the earliest phase it exists in. A zone multiplies the speed (lunge: design.n24.wyrm.speed.lungeMult and head contact design.n24.wyrm.contact.lunge) between two waypoints. The dive's hidden leg is underground (y below the floor): its length sets the 'erupts from a marked wall spot about 4 s later' of the design. Generated by a script, then read by Wyrm; the numbers that are not positions are in design.n24.wyrm.",
